experiment: glide
  instrument        glide   trial seed 000000000135461a   1200000 ticks
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  seed family       offset 730151 -> first creature 0000000001404bf0 (FRESH: nothing
                    has been measured on these seeds)
  the observation   `struct Word` is three scalars and every caregiver render
                    in this codebase passes constants, so NOTHING THIS
                    CREATURE HAS EVER HEARD CHANGES WHILE SOUNDING. A long
                    line of work asked whether the brain can GENERATE a
                    sequence; none asked whether it can FOLLOW one.
  the rate is DERIVED, and the derivation refuses the obvious design. The
    formant path is one-pole with tau = smoothing_ms = 800 ms exactly, corner
    0.199 Hz. A human diphthong (150-250 ms) passes at |H| 0.06-0.10, so a
    460 Hz heard sweep would arrive as 27-45 Hz of produced travel -- below
    the noise floor. Run at that rate, a flat voice would have been written up
    as `the route carries only steady state`, refuting the wrong thing:
    NO AMOUNT OF LEARNING FIXES A FILTER.
  so the arms are   slow 4000 ms (|H| 0.85, 390 Hz), mid 1600 ms (0.54,
                    247 Hz), fast 400 ms (0.16, 72 Hz). `fast` is an
                    INSTRUMENT CHECK, not a hypothesis.
  artefact EXCLUDED, not controlled. `framecopy` looked spectacular and was
    the shipped inhibitory auditory->vocal tract gating babble off while the
    creature heard something -- a reflex copies ANY envelope. So THE
    CAREGIVER'S AMPLITUDE IS CONSTANT here and only the formant moves. There
    is no envelope at f to copy. Produced amplitude is scored at f anyway as a
    trip-wire.
  what it CANNOT claim: at 1.6-4 s this is a slowly moving vowel, not a
    diphthong, so it says nothing about syllable-rate imitation.

  PRE-REGISTERED
    vacuity guard   the `hear` arms must show a LOWER duty than `silent-mid`.
                    The listening reflex is documented; if duty is unchanged
                    the caregiver is not arriving and nothing else reads.
    FOLLOW          `glide-mid` F1-SNR >= 2.0 AND >= 3 SE over `static-mid`,
                    with `f2glide-mid` and `silent-mid` at the static
                    baseline. The voice tracks a heard trajectory.
    REFUSAL         `glide-mid` at the static baseline -> the auditory->vocal
                    route carries no timbre, and the sequence problem is
                    confirmed INTERNAL. A real refusal, not a null.
    trip-wire       produced AMPLITUDE SNR at f should stay at the static
                    baseline in every arm. If it rises with F1, something
                    couples and the F1 reading is suspect.
    instrument      expect slow >= mid > fast if the 800 ms pole is the
                    limit. A FLAT profile across rates would mean the
                    statistic is not measuring following.
    honest prior    `vocallearn` cuts error +24 toward a FIXED target and
                    -0.1 toward a HEARD one, so imitation is already a
                    documented null. This run carries NO REWARD: it asks
                    whether the echo exists, not whether reward can chase it.

